<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eurybiades</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/480-bce">480 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eurybiades was the Spartan admiral who commanded the allied Greek fleet during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a>' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a> in 480 BCE. Although the Athenian contingent was by far the largest, the allies insisted on a Spartan commander. Persuaded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a>, he fought at Artemisium and then at Salamis, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> defeated the Persian fleet.</p></div>
